 "revision3": "### Lead ruling (bq), 2026-11-07: RSL revision 3, limited to two demonstrable errors (LIB0_ F1, F2)\n\nUnder (bp)(4) the specs change only on a demonstrable error against the frozen source. LIB0_ (evidence/lib-map-20261107/LIB0_MAP.md) shows two: (F1) heap::filled/uninit (crates r0/heap.rs:5-14 at 4bb3b3f) return Err(Allocation) when the reservation fails, but RSL Env has no channel for that outcome, so the laws for filled, accNew, weightsNew, claims and tx2auth are relational and A1 is unprovable (AMN a1_forces_det). Fix: add a reservation reply to Env, bound to the headline reservation binder. (F2) TX1:179's CLOSED root requires canonical y1 values; frozen prepare never checks them; RowSpec_087's domain lacks the clause. Fix: own-input clause R4 on 087, recorded as a caller clause and discharged in 094 by canonical_scan. Nothing else changes; F3 (179 Err arm), F4 (332 allocation site), F6 (186 allocation), F7 (finishInputDom), F8 (130 mark with obs Some) are missing child lemmas provable from the existing child proofs and belong to LIB_. Target not yet established.\nRuling (bq) clarification, 2026-11-07 (LIBB_ module 12 query): the rev3 gate on the five F1 laws (filled, accNew, weightsNew, claims, tx2auth) is RETURNED-VALUE functionality, as RSL_REVISION3.md line 51 states (\"abort arms do not return a value, so they do not affect returned-value determinism\", which is all a1_forces_det needs): for every env, at most one RETURNED observation (Ok or Err with its value and events); abort and independently stopped prefix observations permitted by (bl)(3) may coexist. The strict Spec.Functional (one observation including aborts) is stronger than the gate and is NOT required; a returned-arm form (ReturnFunctional) defined in a LIB module and proved for each of the five laws discharges the gate. This is an interpretation of the existing frozen text, not a spec change. Target not yet established.",
 "superseded_claim": "Revision 1 `TX1_328.rejects_silent` rejected every event-free outcome at k \u2260 10, including the constant abort",
 "superseded_status": "SUPERSEDED; reporting and proof correction, no protocol change",
 "replacement": "rejects_silentRet and ref_admits_abort; abort writes nothing and accepts nothing",
