 "revision4_verbatim": "### Lead ruling (bs), 2026-11-07: RSL revision 4, one demonstrable error (TX1:094 public length)\n\nNNG_ (evidence/tx1-principal-20261111/NNG_HANDOFF.md) found that the CLOSED TX1:186 checkpoint law installed in the library requires public_bytes.length = 1880, which RowSpec_094's Domain does not contain; frozen tx1 never checks it, and first_decoded (programs/r1-cost-probe/src/lib.rs, frozen 4bb3b3f) passes public_bytes through unchecked. The length is guaranteed upstream: stage1 snapshots the public account at POOL_V1_PAIR_FOREST_TERMINAL_STATEMENT_BYTES (r1_pool_adapter_owned.rs:453), and snapshot copies only an exact-length account. Fix (same shape as rev3 R4): add own-input clause P1880 (public_bytes.length = 1880) to RowSpec_094's Domain under (bf)(2); record it as caller clause at TX1:328 (RowSpec_328 Domain gains the same clause, since first_decoded passes the bytes unchanged) and discharge it in TX1:345 from the snapshot length (the 345 owned public account data has length 1880 on every path that reaches first_decoded). Nothing else changes. Target not yet established.\n\n",
 "owner_condition4_20261108_verbatim": "### Owner decision 2026-11-08: discharge strategy for condition (4) by pointwise inclusion (recorded by the lead)\n\nOwner, on INP_REPORT.md section 1.5: approved. Condition (4) may be discharged by proving, for EVERY oracle O and EVERY choice of adversary randomness r (adaptive behaviour included), Failure(O,r) implies ChargedEvent(O,r), and then applying the existing bound: Pr[Failure] <= Pr[ChargedEvent] <= the adopted bound. A separate bound per fixed oracle is not required; the bound applies to the complete experiment. Non-negotiable: (1) the inclusion concerns the ACTUAL adversary's execution (pair instantiated from it, Realizes by construction), not an arbitrary pair or an abstract model whose connection is assumed; (2) both events live on the SAME probability space (all oracle outcomes and adversary randomness), with no conditioning, discarded outcomes or restriction of adaptive adversaries; (3) the existing bound applies to EXACTLY that charged event, with no additional probability assumption or hidden loss factor. Condition (4) is NOT to be marked proved until the pointwise inclusion and its connection to the existing bound are formally established, and closing this probability step does not establish the source/native correspondence or full deployed soundness. Implementation: INP_ deployed_outer (pointwise domination via RSL.EVB.no_second_charge and TASB.fail_sub_rec) plus NNH_RecordedCharge.bound and the failureModel <= total chain at a := normalize a.\nLead reading (recorded with INP_): the A1 Err clause needs only \"model reply is not Ok\" (game (d) commits only on .ok (.Ok ...)); the decoder-liveness work is not required.\n",
